! =============================================================================
! Tutorial Problem #4 (manual): Aluminum-Magnesium Alloys
! =============================================================================
! System: Al-Mg, Alloy 5252 (Al-2.5wt%Mg), 550 C, 1 atm.
! Teaching point: determine the solidus (onset melting) temperature of an
! alloy without reading it off a binary phase diagram -- useful once the
! system has more components than a diagram can show.
!
! Run:    ./bin/InputScriptMode inputs/training/manual/tut04_AlMg_alloy_solidus.ti
! Verified output: 3.7164 mol FCC_A1 (single phase, no liquid) at 550 C.
! Sweep temperature upward (see tut04_sweep.ti) to find the solidus: a second
! phase (Liquid) first appears between 620 C and 625 C, matching the manual's
! reported solidus of 620 C.
! =============================================================================
temperature       = 550
pressure          = 1.0
mass(13)          = 3.6135
mass(12)          = 0.10286
temperature unit  = C
pressure unit     = atm
mass unit         = moles
data file         = data/AlMg-Liang.dat
print mode        = 2
